        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', 'A linear equation in two variables ax + by + c = 0 has how many real solutions?', '{"A":"A unique solution","B":"Only two solutions","C":"Infinitely many solutions","D":"No solution"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'MCQ', 'Mathematics', 'Linear Equations in Two Variables', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Every point lying on the straight line represented by the equation is a solution; thus it possesses infinitely many solutions.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-000000000008', 'According to Euclid''s Axiom 1, things which are equal to the same thing are:', '{"A":"Double of each other","B":"Half of each other","C":"Equal to one another","D":"Perpendicular"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'MCQ', 'Mathematics', 'Introduction to Euclid''s Geometry', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Euclid''s First Axiom: ''Things which are equal to the same thing are also equal to one another.''', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'If two complementary angles are in the ratio 2 : 3, what is the measure of the smaller angle?', '{"A":"36°","B":"54°","C":"30°","D":"45°"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'Mathematics', 'Lines and Angles', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Complementary angles sum to 90°. Let angles be 2x and 3x. 2x + 3x = 90° -> 5x = 90° -> x = 18°. Smaller angle = 2 * 18° = 36°.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a', 'In triangle ABC, if AB = AC and angle B = 50°, then angle A is:', '{"A":"50°","B":"80°","C":"100°","D":"65°"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'Mathematics', 'Triangles', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Since AB = AC, ∠C = ∠B = 50° (angles opposite to equal sides are equal). By angle sum property: ∠A = 180° - (50° + 50°) = 80°.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b', 'Express 0.2353535... (i.e. 0.235 with bar on 35) in the p/q form, where p and q are integers and q ≠ 0.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Mathematics', 'Number Systems', 2, 'Let x = 0.2353535... Multiplying by 10: 10x = 2.353535... (Eq 1). Multiplying by 1000: 1000x = 235.353535... (Eq 2). Subtracting Eq 1 from Eq 2: 990x = 233 -> x = 233 / 990.', '1 Mark for setting up equations with appropriate multipliers 10 and 1000; 1 Mark for subtraction and final simplified fraction 233/990', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c', 'Find the value of the polynomial p(y) = 2 + y + 2y² - y³ at: (i) y = 0, (ii) y = 2.', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Mathematics', 'Polynomials', 2, '(i) p(0) = 2 + 0 + 2(0)² - (0)³ = 2. (ii) p(2) = 2 + 2 + 2(2)² - (2)³ = 4 + 8 - 8 = 4.', '1 Mark for calculating p(0) = 2; 1 Mark for calculating p(2) = 4', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d', 'In which quadrants or on which axes do the following points lie: A(0, -4), B(-2, 3), C(5, 0), D(4, -3)?', NULL, NULL, 'VSA', 'Mathematics', 'Coordinate Geometry', 2, 'A(0, -4) lies on the negative y-axis. B(-2, 3) lies in Quadrant II. C(5, 0) lies on the positive x-axis. D(4, -3) lies in Quadrant IV.', '0.5 Mark for each correctly identified quadrant/axis location (total 2 Marks)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e', 'Rationalise the denominator of: 1 / (7 + 3√2).', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Mathematics', 'Number Systems', 3, 'Multiplying numerator and denominator by conjugate (7 - 3√2): [1 * (7 - 3√2)] / [(7 + 3√2)(7 - 3√2)] = (7 - 3√2) / [7² - (3√2)²] = (7 - 3√2) / [49 - (9 * 2)] = (7 - 3√2) / (49 - 18) = (7 - 3√2) / 31.', '1 Mark for identifying conjugate; 1 Mark for denominator difference of squares (49 - 18); 1 Mark for final rationalized fraction', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f', 'Factorise completely using the identity: 27x³ + y³ + z³ - 9xyz.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Mathematics', 'Polynomials', 3, 'Rewrite as: (3x)³ + y³ + z³ - 3(3x)(y)(z). Using identity a³ + b³ + c³ - 3abc = (a + b + c)(a² + b² + c² - ab - bc - ca) where a = 3x, b = y, c = z: = (3x + y + z)[(3x)² + y² + z² - (3x)(y) - y(z) - z(3x)] = (3x + y + z)(9x² + y² + z² - 3xy - yz - 3zx).', '1 Mark for recognizing cubic identity; 1 Mark for substitution of terms; 1 Mark for expanded second polynomial factor', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-000000000010', 'Draw the graph of the linear equation 2x + y = 6. Find the coordinates of the points where the line crosses the coordinate axes.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Mathematics', 'Linear Equations in Two Variables', 3, 'Find solutions: When x = 0, y = 6 -> (0, 6). When y = 0, 2x = 6 -> x = 3 -> (3, 0). When x = 1, y = 4 -> (1, 4). Plotting these points on graph and drawing a line through them gives the graph. The line crosses the x-axis at (3, 0) and the y-axis at (0, 6).', '1 Mark for finding table of three points; 1 Mark for plotting straight line graph; 1 Mark for identifying intercepts (3, 0) and (0, 6)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-000000000011', 'The length, breadth, and height of a room are 8 m 25 cm, 6 m 75 cm, and 4 m 50 cm respectively. Determine the longest tape which can measure the three dimensions of the room exactly.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'Mathematics', 'Number Systems', 5, 'Convert all dimensions into centimeters: Length l = 825 cm, Breadth b = 675 cm, Height h = 450 cm. The length of the longest tape is given by the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of 825, 675, and 450. Prime factorisations: 825 = 3 * 5² * 11. 675 = 3³ * 5². 450 = 2 * 3² * 5². HCF(825, 675, 450) = 3¹ * 5² = 3 * 25 = 75 cm. Hence, the longest measuring tape required is 75 cm (or 0.75 m).', '1.5 Marks for unit conversion to cm; 2 Marks for prime factorisation of numbers; 1.5 Marks for finding HCF = 75 cm', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020017-0000-4000-8000-000000000012', 'Answer the following: (i) Calculate the slant height ''l'' of the conical tent. (ii) Find the area of canvas required to erect the tent (excluding the floor). (iii) Find the total cost of canvas fabric required.', NULL, NULL, 'CASE', 'Mathematics', 'Surface Areas and Volumes', 4, '(i) Slant height l = √(r² + h²) = √(7² + 24²) = √(49 + 576) = √625 = 25 meters. (ii) Canvas required = Curved Surface Area = πrl = (22/7) * 7 * 25 = 22 * 25 = 550 m². (iii) Total cost = Area * Rate = 550 * 70 = ₹ 38,500.', '1 Mark for slant height l = 25 m; 2 Marks for curved surface area 550 m²; 1 Mark for total cost ₹ 38,500', 'A residential welfare society constructed a conical canvas tent to serve as a community health camp. The radius of the base of the conical tent is 7 m, and its vertical height is 24 m. The canvas fabric used costs ₹ 70 per square meter.', NULL, 'MEDIUM', true)
