        ('90020025-0000-4000-8000-000000000008', 'Rationalise the denominator of: 1 / (7 + 3√2).', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Mathematics', 'Number Systems', 3, 'Multiplying numerator and denominator by conjugate (7 - 3√2): [1 * (7 - 3√2)] / [(7 + 3√2)(7 - 3√2)] = (7 - 3√2) / [7² - (3√2)²] = (7 - 3√2) / [49 - (9 * 2)] = (7 - 3√2) / (49 - 18) = (7 - 3√2) / 31.', '1 Mark for identifying conjugate; 1 Mark for denominator difference of squares (49 - 18); 1 Mark for final rationalized fraction', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020025-0000-4000-8000-000000000009', 'Factorise completely using the identity: 27x³ + y³ + z³ - 9xyz.', NULL, NULL, 'SA', 'Mathematics', 'Polynomials', 3, 'Rewrite as: (3x)³ + y³ + z³ - 3(3x)(y)(z). Using identity a³ + b³ + c³ - 3abc = (a + b + c)(a² + b² + c² - ab - bc - ca) where a = 3x, b = y, c = z: = (3x + y + z)[(3x)² + y² + z² - (3x)(y) - y(z) - z(3x)] = (3x + y + z)(9x² + y² + z² - 3xy - yz - 3zx).', '1 Mark for recognizing cubic identity; 1 Mark for substitution of terms; 1 Mark for expanded second polynomial factor', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90020025-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a', '(a) Factorise the cubic polynomial: p(x) = x³ - 23x² + 142x - 120. (b) Verify by using factor theorem and polynomial long division.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'Mathematics', 'Polynomials', 5, 'Constant term is -120. Factors of -120 include ±1, ±2, etc. Testing x = 1: p(1) = 1³ - 23(1)² + 142(1) - 120 = 1 - 23 + 142 - 120 = 143 - 143 = 0. Therefore, (x - 1) is a factor. Dividing p(x) by (x - 1): x³ - 23x² + 142x - 120 = (x - 1)(x² - 22x + 120). Splitting the middle term of quotient: x² - 22x + 120 = x² - 12x - 10x + 120 = x(x - 12) - 10(x - 12) = (x - 12)(x - 10). Complete factorisation: p(x) = (x - 1)(x - 10)(x - 12).', '1.5 Marks for finding initial root x=1 via factor theorem; 2 Marks for long division to get quadratic x² - 22x + 120; 1.5 Marks for splitting middle term into (x - 10)(x - 12)', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true)
